{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>You shall not go about as a talebearer.</b> I say that the name is because all who send strife and tellers of evil tongue who go about in the houses of their fellows to spy out what evil they may see, or what evil they may hear, to tell in the market, are called הוֹלְכֵי רָכִיל — goers of spying, אשפיי״מנט בְּלַעַ״ז. And a proof to my words: we do not find רְכִילוּת that is not written in the language of going — לֹא תֵלֵךְ רָכִיל, הוֹלְכֵי רָכִיל נְחֹשֶׁת וּבַרְזֶל (Jeremiah 6), and the rest of evil tongue is not written in it 'going' — מְלָשְׁנִי בַסֵּתֶר רֵעֵהוּ (Psalms 101), לָשׁוֹן רְמִיָּה (ibid. 120), לָשׁוֹן מְדַבֶּרֶת גְּדֹלוֹת (ibid. 12). Therefore I say that the tongue goes and spies — that the כַּ\"ף is interchanged with גִימֶ״ל, for all the letters whose place of articulation is one are interchanged with one another: בֵּי\"ת with פֵ\"א, and גִימֶ\"ל with כַּ\"ף and קוֹ\"ף, and נוּ\"ן with לָמֶ\"ד, and זַיִ\"ן with צָדִ\"י. And so וַיְרַגֵּל בְּעַבְדְּךָ (II Samuel 19) — he spied in deceit to speak evil of me; and so לֹא רָגַל עַל לְשֹׁנוֹ (Psalms 15); and so רוֹכֵל — the merchant who spies after all merchandise; and so one who sells perfumes for women to adorn themselves with them — because he circulates constantly through the towns, he is called רוֹכֵל, language of רוֹגֵל. לָא תֵיכוּל קוּרְצִין, like וַאֲכַלוּ קַרְצֵיהוֹן דִּי יְהוּדָיֵא (Daniel 3:8), אָכַל בֵּיהּ קוּרְצָא בֵּי מַלְכָּא (Berakhot 58a). It appears to me that their practice was to eat in the house that receives their words some stuffing of food, and it is the conclusion of corroboration that his words are upheld and he establishes them as truth, and that stuffing is called אֲכִילַת קוּרְצִין — language of קוֹרֵץ בְּעֵינָיו (Proverbs 6), for so is the way of all הוֹלְכֵי רָכִיל to wink with their eyes and to signal words of their רְכִילוּת, so that the rest of the hearers will not understand." "<b>Nor shall you stand upon the blood of your fellow.</b> To watch his death when you are able to save him — for example, one drowning in a river, or robbers coming upon him (Sanhedrin 73a)." "<b>I am YHWH.</b> Faithful to pay reward, and faithful to exact punishment."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "the la'az אשפיי״מנט is Old French espionement, 'spying'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:19.101308934Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}